build-downgrade/build-downgrade/README.md:1:# The Classics Never Go Out of Style: An Empirical Study of Downgrades from the Bazel Build Technology
build-downgrade/build-downgrade/README.md:5:This replication package enables the replication of the study "The Classics Never Go Out of Style: An Empirical Study of Downgrades from the Bazel Build Technology", accepted to ICSE2024. The study explores the phenomenon of build system downgrades, i.e., projects that move from a feature-rich modern build tool to a more traditional one (e.g., Bazel to Make). Surprisingly, the paper shows that, in the context of Bazel, downgrades happen regularly—roughly 11.2% of the studied projects that adopted Bazel downgraded to a less feature-rich alternative. The study also characterizes downgrades according to seven emergent themes, analyzed what tools replaced Bazel in the downgrading projects, and studied the generalizability of the themes using a confirmatory context (downgrades from Gradle) and a contradictory context (upgrades to Bazel).
build-downgrade/build-downgrade/README.md:26:- *study-output*: holds results that will be produced after running the package. The folder will produce the following outputs:
build-downgrade/build-downgrade/README.md:28:   - `current.csv`: holds data related to projects that adopt the Bazel build system. This file can be seen under the `results` folder after running the docker images.
build-downgrade/build-downgrade/README.md:29:   - `abandoned.csv`: holds data related to projects that abandoned the Bazel build system. This file can be seen under the `results` folder after running the docker images.
