<sst xmlns="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/spreadsheetml/2006/main" count="302" uniqueCount="178"><si><t>https://github.com/chromium/subspace/commit/24f7dd6ed3857f72573051fd52e17e5b707a86e4</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/hachibu/dotfiles/commit/7c4db7cb53d195ac655d5393eb7109e393d6fdbc</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/amigneco/advent-of-code.cpp/commit/8795bcc82215b1197f2bdb38f74418792a0a8322</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/CodeIntelligenceTesting/cifuzz/pull/735</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/emer/axon/pull/68</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/kopeio/networking/pull/85</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/dasch-swiss/dsp-tangoh-app/pull/56</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/gardener/apiserver-proxy/pull/25</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/cloudspannerecosystem/wrench/pull/68</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/joneshf/terraform-provider-openwrt/pull/3</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/istio/test-infra/commit/b7b5032ee0b5b18be4a2f09f5114d6bc97ac285a</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/openshift/machine-api-operator/commit/f53ed329ffc4cc0841e1b8145cc63877ddff4ac4</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/kubernetes/cloud-provider-gcp/pull/259</t></si><si><t>removal-ref</t></si><si><t>replaced-by</t></si><si><t>Comment(s)</t></si><si><t>NA</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/bufbuild/connect-swift/commit/4198991b63ee6fae661d1a83637dcc8370dcdd47</t></si><si><t>Swift PM</t></si><si><t>CMake</t></si><si><t>Gradle</t></si><si><t>SBT</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/swift-nav/yaml-cpp/commit/5665589c364cc5134ce10f3adf02310712bbc09c</t></si><si><t>Go build</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/LibreCybernetics/Monorepo/pull/52/commits/cda23a16f3648bd8368bd707b9e83ecb19140910</t></si><si><t>Make</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/google/trillian/pull/2743</t></si><si><t>Build failures: Bazel has more issues when used at small scale, like specific part of the project on specific platforms.</t></si><si><t>Build failures.</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kubefed/commit/535c0071a45727fa32bade3b4deb05967eb86418</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/kubernetes/org/commit/5ccc77c23059aea59aabb43c0d24eb95393398c0</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/maistra/istio/commit/9ab21461969d1cfe6276c759fc27be64d4641137</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/markphelps/flipt/commit/3a9fa2407dda2a3fcbe15418b132dff25ed1a3bf</t></si><si><t>T3</t></si><si><t>Difficulty in maintainability and troubleshooting</t></si><si><t>T1, T2</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/cluster-api/issues/660
https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/cluster-api/pull/1321</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/flipt-io/flipt/tree/main/build</t></si><si><t>T2, T6</t></si><si><t>T2</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/wardle/concierge-old/commit/458e3519eadc76512101097da2770f8a451f57e4
https://github.com/wardle/concierge-old/commit/9c31c7f50c3642bd5ef3604abd222463ae781dc0</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/berty/berty/pull/2127/commits/14a03463751db6bc7514964d12444e3c42be87c4</t></si><si><t>T1</t></si><si><t xml:space="preserve">Maintaing two build systems is hard, and they chose to use the simpler/typical build system like CMake. </t></si><si><t>"I'd like to put this idea out there: we should ditch bazel builds for now.

Reason: they don't work, and go 1.10 has made incremental builds much faster for local dev, while circleci 2.0 has made the CI much faster. So the only thing they add is being able to detect exactly which image has changed and only push / deploy that. Personally, even if that was the case, I'd probably still want all the cortex images to be pushed at the same version, to make it easy to see that they are all up to date.

WDYT?

(This does somewhat pain me, I like bazel, but go has come far enough to make the gains not worth the effort IMO)"</t></si><si><t>T4</t></si><si><t>"now that this is not used as a submodule of obelisk, we can rely on gazelle to auto-generate the bazel files that obelisk needs to build this."</t></si><si><t>A dependency is no longer required</t></si><si><t>T5</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/emer/emergent/pull/106/commits
https://github.com/emer/emergent/commit/968d99139d760df83442ef2c5e34c654064306e4</t></si><si><t>"now that there is no cyclic dependency between this and emer/emergent, should not be needed"</t></si><si><t>https://github.com/emer/empi/pull/4
https://github.com/emer/empi/pull/3</t></si><si><t>"the goal is to make it easier to work with the LLVM subproject MLIR.
LLVM technically has some bazel support, but in practice, it is very fragile and our team wasn't even able to get it working with the MLIR subproject in particular. 
We would prefer to be able to directly build the project instead of having to link a prebuilt tar like what you're currently doing for LLVM (without MLIR)."</t></si><si><t>T6</t></si><si><t>Breakages and errors</t></si><si><t>Follow upstream repos</t></si><si><t>T8</t></si><si><t>"CMake is more widely used and familiar to our dev team.
